 evidence-uncertainty is genuinely high; report accuracy drop vs. lag threshold, and characterize cases where the fresh estimate is itself overconfident (underthinking risk). 7) Generalization: transfer probes and refresh trigger across datasets and model scales without retraining.", 'Risk Factors and Limitations': "The distinction between 'gating' and 'evidence' uncertainty relies on read-position choices that may be entangled; if the two probes are not separable, the lag framing weakens (an informative negative result). Confidence probes are noisy for open-ended answers, so we focus on math/multiple-choice with extractable answers. The stale-uncertainty hypothesis may be wrong — reflection could be a deliberate learned exploration strategy rather than an update failure — which would still yield a publishable mechanistic characterization. The uncertainty-refresh patch alters internal state and may introduce new errors or overconfidence, causing underthinking on hard items; the evidence-uncertainty threshold aims to guard against this. Intervention gains may not exceed strong steering baselines, but the lag diagnosis is a standalone contribution. Results may be model-family specific and vary non-monotonically with scale."}

